# umbrella.gitignore.example — reference layout for a SHARED SPEC REPOSITORY.
#
# When you run `./harness-install.sh --umbrella <dir> --shared-repo`, the installer
# generates the real umbrella-root .gitignore for you (append-only) — it ignores the
# product child repos it discovered plus per-developer agent state. This file just
# documents the intended shape so you can read or hand-tune it.
#
# The umbrella root is its OWN git repo (a "spec repository") that TRACKS the shared
# planning state — .harness/ (specs, state/tasks.json, progress) and the umbrella docs
# (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, README.md, …) — and IGNORES everything that belongs elsewhere.

# --- Product repos: each is its own git repo, cloned INTO the umbrella. ---
# Tracked separately (never as gitlinks here). The installer lists the dirs it found;
# add new ones here as you clone them. Examples:
#/your-api/
#/your-frontend/
#/your-infra/

# --- Assets that are not (yet) their own repo and shouldn't live in the spec repo. ---
#/design-system/

# --- Per-developer / runtime agent state — never shared. ---
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# Per-tool MCP scratch dirs your setup may create — add your own (example):
#.playwright-mcp/

# --- OS / editor junk ---
.DS_Store
*.swp

# NOTE: the local-only telemetry log (.harness/telemetry.jsonl) is already excluded by
# the nested .harness/.gitignore the installer seeds — no entry needed here.
